You are updating an existing rule-based extractor. Do NOT rewrite good rules; add or adjust only what is needed.

Task: German Legal Named Entity Recognition
Description: Recognize named entities in German legal text. Entities to look for: person. German capitalizes all nouns, so rules must use strong context anchors 

Input schema: {'text': 'str'}
Output schema:
entities: List[Entity]

Entity:
  text: string  # The matched text span
  start: integer  # Start character offset
  end: integer  # End character offset
  type: string  # Entity label

AVAILABLE ENTITY TYPES: ['person']
Rules MUST use one of these types in output_template.


DATA EVIDENCE FROM TRAINING:
- person (15 unique): "Dr. Grohmann", "Dr. Nowotny", "Hon.-Prof. PD Dr. Rassi", "MMag. Sloboda und Dr. Kikinger", "Janina Griesmeyer", "Dr. Bernhard Birek", "Josepha Stra\u00dfmer", "Dr. Gernot Lehner", "Dr. Baumann", "Dr. Veith", "Dr. E. Sol\u00e9", "Dr. Schwarzenbacher", "PhD Horst Siegers", "Mag. Dr. Ralf Heinrich H\u00f6fler", "Sabine Schleckermann"
  Exact pattern: (?:M(?:Mag\. Sloboda und Dr\. Kiking|ag\. Dr\. Ralf Heinrich Höfl)er|Hon\.\-Prof\. PD Dr\. Rassi|Sabine Schleckermann|(?:Dr\. (?:Schwarzenbach|Gernot Lehn)|J(?:anina Griesmey|osepha Straßm))er|Dr\. (?:Bernhard Birek|Nowotny|E\. Solé|Veith)|PhD Horst Siegers|Dr\. (?:Groh|Bau)mann)
  In context: "...Senatspr\u00e4sidentin [Dr. Grohmann] als Vorsitzende...", "...sowie die Hofr\u00e4te [Dr. Nowotny], Hon.-Prof. PD Dr....", "...Dr. Nowotny, [Hon.-Prof. PD Dr. Rassi], MMag. Sloboda und...", "...PD Dr. Rassi, [MMag. Sloboda und Dr. Kikinger] als weitere...", "...klagenden Partei [Janina Griesmeyer], vertreten durch..."

Note: Some entities contain multiple words; do NOT assume single-token matches.

Computed patterns match training strings only; generalize carefully.



RULES with failures (full details, note any user_feedback on specific rules):
[
